  "remaining_limitations": [
    "Not a scan and not an exact likeness: a CC0 MakeHuman base sculpted by hand-tuned deformations and then warped to 19 hand-picked photo landmarks + 5 cheek-contour points + the visible ear, as seen from one camera. Depth (nose/cheek/jaw/skull profile) is inferred, so the profile and back are plausible guesses.",
    "The face texture comes from one bright, beauty-filtered selfie: it is smooth, partly de-lit (low-frequency division only), and some photo shading/makeup remains baked in. Areas the photo never saw (sides/back of head, ears, under the chin, scalp) use a procedural skin layer tinted to the photo's median complexion.",
    "Eyes: the right (far) eye still sits a few pixels off the photo; iris colour comes from the photo but the sclera/cornea are procedural; the eyes read slightly larger and more 'doll-like' than in the photo.",
    "Hair is a procedural guide/child Curves groom (not photo-textured): bangs, ear tuck and waves are approximations, the crown reads a little flat and dark, strand clumping is more regular than real hair, and a white-ish backlit tuft over the left ear plus a few stray strands show in the turntable views.",
    "The 26 mm selfie perspective makes the torso smaller relative to the head than in the reference (hem visible). The torso/collar sits about 60 px (in the 1205 px photo) away from the photographed collar; solving an extra neck rotation for it broke the hair at the nape, so it was not applied.",
    "Sweater is a displaced shell from the posed body (no cloth simulation); knit is a generated height tile with a photo-sampled base colour, not the photographed knit.",
    "Hands/fingers are simple tube + ellipsoid geometry; they are outside the selfie frame (as in the photo) but visible and crude in the turntable views. No production rig.",
    "Turntable views hide the cafe set and use a grey world + one back fill light; the character is identical.",
    "The result is still visibly CG at close inspection (skin micro-detail, eye wetness, hair)."
  ]
}